PATCH 569: the render walk 378e passes BX = the deferred record to its methods; 37cd rebuilt; 3823's CX
is 3d4c's output.

asm 0x37ab-0x37b6: `mov bx,0x6bbe ; xor dx,dx ; mov dl,[0x6bc2] ; mov si,dx ; call [si+0x4b52]` -- every
render method in the 0x4b52 table (3663 390c 3823 37cd 38aa 390d 32a6) is entered with BX = the current
deferred record at DGROUP:0x6bbe.  Patch 194's dispatch was `(*vec)()`: 3823/37cd/38aa's param_3 and
390d's param_1 were stack residue.  It never showed because c33c's producers were unreachable until
patches 556/558 and, after them, the residue happened to be harmless -- until the first AZER1 self-play
with a live T-80 (566/567): the walk hung for ever in the MGA blitter m_mga_298a with a record pointer
of 0xcc08 (next run 0xcc28) -- an address inside vehicle 11's body -- whose "sprite id" word resolved
to a sprite header of width 0, i.e. `loop` x 65536 x 65536.  __allregs is positional and the methods
differ in arity, so the record is passed in all three slots.

37cd (entry 9, method id 0x12 = the id c9af stamps into each record it drains) was pristine: the record
host-deref'd, and 3d4c's Y output taken from the incoming CX.  3823 (patch 391) had the same CX misread:
`3827 call 3d4c` returns the Y projection in CX (`3d94 mov [0x6c38],cx ; ret`), 3830 pushes it and
385b/3893 add it -- an OUTPUT of the call, not an input of the method.  Both now read word[0x6c38]; 38aa
(patch 526) already did.

390d (entry 12, method id 0x18, the two-point 3d99 line) stays pristine in this patch: it is a
different family, was not on the path measured here, and will fault loudly rather than draw garbage
when a producer first emits id 0x18 (board:0015).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -12103,7 +12103,13 @@
      * returned si so word[0x4b9e]!=0 and the phase walk advances instead of restarting. */
     *(uint16_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + 0x4b9e) = g_fist_iter_si;         /* word[0x4b9e]=si (asm 0x37a7) */
     sidx = *(uint8_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + 0x6bc2);                    /* dl=byte[0x6bc2]; si=dx */
-    (*(code *)fist_icall_near(0x0u, *(uint16_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + sidx + 0x4b52)))(); /* [si+0x4b52] */
+    /* PATCH 569: asm 0x37ab `mov bx,0x6bbe` -- every render method in the 0x4b52 table receives BX = the
+     * current deferred RECORD.  The arg-less dispatch left 3823/37cd/38aa's param_3 (and 390d's param_1)
+     * as stack residue: the AZER1 self-play that first drew a T-80 shot hung forever in the MGA blitter
+     * (m_mga 298a) on a record pointer of 0xcc08 / 0xcc28 -- inside vehicle 11's body -- whose "sprite
+     * id" resolved to a zero-width header.  __allregs is positional and the methods differ in arity, so
+     * the record goes in every slot. */
+    ((void (*)(int,int,int))fist_icall_near(0x0u, *(uint16_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + sidx + 0x4b52)))(0x6bbe, 0x6bbe, 0x6bbe); /* [si+0x4b52] */
   }
   ((unsigned short (*)(unsigned short))fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b0)))(saved_mask);
                                                                       /* 37c2 pop ax; 37c3 lcall [0x6b0] */
